cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset or code, please cite the associated article."
title: "Energy-matched lid-drive control classes in a lid-driven cavity: mechanistic case study (Re = 500, E* = 0.25)"
abstract: >-
  Code, data and figures for a focused fixed-energy comparison of four lid-drive
  control classes (uniform, stationary second harmonic, mixed spatio-temporal,
  pure temporal) in a lid-driven cavity at Re = 500, aspect ratio 1, with the
  actuation-energy budget E* = 0.25 held identical across all four controls.
  The study isolates the role of the spatio-temporal structure of the control on
  circulation, strain-rate dissipation, wall shear and the field-mean/fluctuation
  partition. Includes the vendored LBM-MRT solver, the PINN module of the
  companion paper, the 15 PINN seed checkpoints used to build the controls, and
  the full reproduction pipeline with SHA256 verification.
type: software
license: MIT
